@startuml
title Scope extrusion, mechanised: the restriction's containment BEFORE and AFTER the float pass

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #6D28D9
  FontColor #111827
}

package "BEFORE — the restriction binds only its own component" as BEFORE #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "**PPar** — the AC bag\n<latex>\{\,(\nu c)P \;\mid\; Q\,\}</latex>" as B_PAR #DBEAFE {
    rectangle "**PNew**  binder ""c""\nthe restriction's scope" as B_NEW #EDE9FE {
      rectangle "**P**\n""c"" is IN scope here" as B_P #DCFCE7
    }
    rectangle "**Q**\n""c"" is OUT of scope here —\nany ""c"" in Q is a DIFFERENT, free name" as B_Q #FEF3C7
  }
}

package "AFTER — the restriction binds the whole composition" as AFTER #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "**PNew**  binder ""c'"" (FRESH)\nthe restriction's scope" as A_NEW #EDE9FE {
    rectangle "**PPar** — the AC bag\n<latex>(\nu c')\{\,P' \;\mid\; Q\,\}</latex>" as A_PAR #DBEAFE {
      rectangle "**P'**\n= P with ""c"" renamed to ""c'""" as A_P #DCFCE7
      rectangle "**Q**\nUNCHANGED — and now inside\nthe scope of ""c'"", harmlessly,\nbecause ""c'"" is fresh" as A_Q #FEF3C7
    }
  }
}

B_PAR -right[#BE185D,thickness=2]-> A_NEW : **the float pass**\n""Proc::__bcn_float_pass"" —\nsee ""binder_congruence.rs""

note bottom of BEFORE #FEE2E2
  This is the shape the declared equation ""ScopeExt"" names:
  ""(PPar {(PNew ^x.P), ...rest}) = (PNew ^x.(PPar {P, ...rest}))""
  under the premise ""x # ...rest"".

  That equation is **NOT lowered** onto the e-graph: its
  ""Premise::Freshness"" fails ""premise_supported"".
end note

note bottom of AFTER #DCFCE7
  The float discharges the SAME law operationally, and the
  premise ""x # ...rest"" is not TESTED — it is made TRUE.
  ""Scope::unbind"" freshens the binder before the body is
  ever exposed, so the floated restriction cannot capture
  anything in the residual. Freshening ENFORCES the side
  condition that the declarative reading merely ASSUMES.
end note

legend right
|= Region |= Reading |
|<#EDE9FE> violet | the extent of a ""PNew"" restriction — what the binder governs |
|<#DBEAFE> blue | the ""PPar"" AC bag (a ""HashBag"" — unordered, auto-flattening) |
|<#DCFCE7> green | the component the restriction originally bound |
|<#FEF3C7> amber | the residual the restriction is floated PAST |
endlegend

@enduml
